  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for the Integration of Migrants by the Municipality of Agadir and Neighboring Municipalities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to its particular geographical position, at the junction between Europe and Africa, Morocco represents a country of origin, transit and destination for a large number of migrants moving within the continent. Those migrants, all categories included, face a number of challenges that stand in the way of their socio-economic stability, and integration.  Although the Government of Morocco has been reinforcing its efforts towards the socio-economic integration of regularized migrants, numerous challenges remain, amongst others: access to health care, education, accommodation, and humanitarian basic needs, etc. In the case of the Region of Souss-Massa, particularly the city of Agadir, most migrants live in marginalized neighborhoods with limited access to drinking water, health services or decent accommodation.The city of Agadir lacks capacity in terms of human and financial resources to respond to the needs of migrants settled in city.  With this project, IOM aims to assist the Municipality of Agadir as well as relevant local actors to identify gaps in term integration in the urban area making use of an innovative tool, the Urban Diagnostic Tool (UDT), and accordingly to identify concrete initiatives and assist with their implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
